language variant
language en-us
name hal
gender male 40

// CLASSIC — the calm machine of 2001.
//
// The thing everyone misremembers about that voice is that it is not robotic. It
// is soft, warm, unhurried and impeccably polite, and that is exactly what makes
// it frightening: nothing in the delivery ever acknowledges the situation. A
// clipped metallic voice saying those lines would be almost reassuring, because
// you would know what you were dealing with.
//
// So every parameter here pulls AWAY from machinery and toward a very calm
// person. The base is en-us: the performance was Canadian, which sits close
// enough to General American that the vowels are right and far enough from RP
// that it is not the announcer voice.

// MID, AND ALMOST LEVEL. The range is 24 units — the narrowest in the cast apart
// from ancient's zero. Not flat, because flat is a robot; NARROW, because
// nothing being said is urgent, including the things that ought to be. The base
// sits mid-male: he is not deep, and reaching for depth would make him
// threatening, which is the one thing he never sounds.
pitch 108 132

// WARM AND CLOSE, WITH NO EDGE ANYWHERE.
// The peak is at 700 Hz, low enough to read as chest and reassurance, and the
// curve falls away steadily above 2 kHz so there is no sibilance and no glare.
// The 1.6 kHz point stays up because his diction is immaculate — every syllable
// is fully formed, and that precision is a large part of the effect. A voice this
// gentle that you can nevertheless understand perfectly is uncanny in a way that
// a gentle mumble is not.
tone 240 195 700 240 1600 185 2400 115 3600 60

// An open, unstrained tract. No formant is peaked hard — nothing about this
// voice is pressed, ever.
formant 0 100 126 130
formant 1 104 124 128
formant 2 106 118 120
formant 3 104 110 106
formant 4  99 102  88
formant 5  92  92  64
formant 6  84  82  40
formant 7  78  76  26
formant 8  74  72  18

// BREATH, AND ABSOLUTE STEADINESS.
// The paradox of the voice, in two lines. breath is generous — he sounds like he
// is at ease, and ease is why the politeness reads as sincere. But flutter is 0
// and roughness is 0: there is not one irregular moment anywhere. A human voice
// under stress wavers; this one physically cannot, and that is the tell.
breath  2 3 4 4 4 4 3 2
breathw 100 135 150 150 150 150 135 105
voicing 76
roughness 0
flutter 0

// Consonants precise but soft — released fully, never struck. He articulates
// like someone who has all the time in the world, because he does.
consonants 78 74

// A small dry room: a speaker in a cabin, not a hall. The point is proximity —
// he is always closer than you would like.
echo 60 9

// NOTHING IS EVER EMPHASISED, AND THAT IS THE HORROR.
// stressAmp barely moves across the whole range and stressAdd is a gentle even
// ramp. He does not lean on a single word — not on "afraid", not on "Dave" — and
// the refusal to emphasise anything is what makes the calm read as absolute
// rather than merely composed. intonation 1 keeps the natural melody: he is
// courteous, not withholding.
intonation 1
stressAmp   14 14 15 15 16 16 17 17
stressAdd    0  5 11 17 23 29 36  43
